> Module Section68
> Using Definitions as W
> Using Section2 as S2

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ApplicableAmount:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input period content W.TaxPeriod
  filing scope S2.FilingStatusFor
  output amount content money

declaration scope ItemizedDeductionLimit:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input period content W.TaxPeriod
  input adjusted_gross_income content money
  input itemized_deductions content money
  applicable scope ApplicableAmount
  output allowed content money
  output reduction content money
```

§68. Overall limitation on itemized deductions

(a) General rule

In the case of an individual whose adjusted gross income exceeds the applicable amount, the amount of the itemized deductions otherwise allowable for the taxable year shall be reduced by the lesser of-


```catala
scope ItemizedDeductionLimit:
  definition applicable.world equals world
  definition applicable.taxpayer equals taxpayer
  definition applicable.period equals period
  definition reduction equals
    if suspended of period
       or adjusted_gross_income <= applicable.amount
    then $0
    else
      let first equals
        three_percent_excess of adjusted_gross_income, applicable.amount in
      let second equals eighty_percent_itemized of itemized_deductions in
      if first <= second then first else second
  definition allowed equals itemized_deductions - reduction
```

    (1) 3 percent of the excess of adjusted gross income over the applicable amount, or


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section68:b0004; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section68(a)(1); source-lines: 7-7; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration three_percent_excess content money
  depends on adjusted_gross_income content money,
             applicable_amount content money
  equals
    if adjusted_gross_income <= applicable_amount
    then $0
    else 3% * (adjusted_gross_income - applicable_amount)
```

    (2) 80 percent of the amount of the itemized deductions otherwise allowable for such taxable year.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section68:b0005; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section68(a)(2); source-lines: 9-9; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration eighty_percent_itemized content money
  depends on itemized_deductions content money
  equals 80% * itemized_deductions
```

(b) Applicable amount

    (1) In general

    For purposes of this section, the term "applicable amount" means-


```catala
scope ApplicableAmount:
  definition filing.world equals world
  definition filing.taxpayer equals taxpayer
  definition filing.period equals period
  definition amount equals applicable_amount_for_status of filing.status
```

        (A) $300,000 in the case of a joint return or a surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section68:b0007; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section68(b)(1)(A); source-lines: 17-17; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration joint_or_surviving_applicable_amount content money
  equals $300000
```

        (B) $275,000 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)),


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section68:b0008; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section68(b)(1)(B); source-lines: 19-19; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration head_of_household_applicable_amount content money
  equals $275000
```

        (C) $250,000 in the case of an individual who is not married and who is not a surviving spouse or head of household, and


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section68:b0009; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section68(b)(1)(C); source-lines: 21-21; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration unmarried_applicable_amount content money
  equals $250000
```

        (D) 1/2 the amount applicable under subparagraph (A) in the case of a married individual filing a separate return.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section68:b0010; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section68(b)(1)(D); source-lines: 23-23; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration married_separate_applicable_amount content money
  equals 50% * joint_or_surviving_applicable_amount
```

    For purposes of this paragraph, marital status shall be determined under section 7703.


```catala
declaration applicable_amount_for_status content money
  depends on status content S2.FilingStatus
  equals match status with pattern
    -- S2.FilingStatus.JointOrSurviving:
        joint_or_surviving_applicable_amount
    -- S2.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold:
        head_of_household_applicable_amount
    -- S2.FilingStatus.Unmarried:
        unmarried_applicable_amount
    -- S2.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately:
        married_separate_applicable_amount
```

(f) Section not to apply

This section shall not apply to any taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017, and before January 1, 2026.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section68:b0012; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section68(f); source-lines: 27-29; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration suspended content boolean
  depends on period content W.TaxPeriod
  equals period.tax_year >= 2018 and period.tax_year <= 2025
```
